                                          2234  #-----------------------------------------------------------------------
                                          2235  #
                                          2236  #  vCPU extension functions (for acceleration and compaction) follow below.
                                          2237  #
                                          2238  #  The naming convention is: SYS_<CamelCase>[_v<V>]_<N>
                                          2239  #
                                          2240  #  With <N> the maximum number of cycles the function will run
                                          2241  #  (counted from NEXT to NEXT). This is the same number that must
                                          2242  #  be passed to the 'SYS' vCPU instruction as operand, and it will
                                          2243  #  appear in the GCL code upon use.
                                          2244  #
                                          2245  #  If a SYS extension got introduced after ROM v1, the version number of
                                          2246  #  introduction is included in the name. This helps the programmer to be
                                          2247  #  reminded to verify the acutal ROM version and fail gracefully on older
                                          2248  #  ROMs than required. See also Docs/GT1-files.txt on using [romType].
                                          2249  #
                                          2250  #-----------------------------------------------------------------------
                                          2251
